		<div class="has_eae_slider elementor-element elementor-element-955a7c0 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child" data-eae-slider="349" data-id="955a7c0" data-element_type="container">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-7d8215b elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="7d8215b" data-element_type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<p>Quantitative fluorescence microscopy requires knowing how much light reaches the sample.<br />In practice, this is not always straightforward. Instrument settings do not directly provide the intensity delivered at the sample plane, and spatial illumination patterns can vary across systems, wavelengths, and imaging conditions.</p>								</div>
				</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
		<div class="has_eae_slider elementor-element elementor-element-4d6d378 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-eae-slider="42453" data-id="4d6d378" data-element_type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
		<div class="has_eae_slider elementor-element elementor-element-f8d88f9 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child" data-eae-slider="4305" data-id="f8d88f9" data-element_type="container">
				</div>
		<div class="has_eae_slider elementor-element elementor-element-ac076df e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child" data-eae-slider="3687" data-id="ac076df" data-element_type="container">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-640e4f1 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="640e4f1" data-element_type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<p><a href="https://csl.sony.fr/people/alienor-lahlou/">Aliénor </a>developed fluorescence-based protocols that use organic dyes and fluorescent proteins as actinometers to measure light intensity directly in microscopy systems. The approach can be used to characterize both illumination intensity and spatial light distribution, and to support calibration across instruments and light sources.</p><p> </p><p><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/1f97d.png" alt="🥽" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> <a href="https://www.protocols.io/view/calibrating-a-blue-light-source-with-dronpa-2-eq2ly4kdrlx9/v1">Protocol</a><br /><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LaIoRGnTDQ0"><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/1f4fd.png" alt="📽" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> Video</a><br /><a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41592-023-02063-y"><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/1f5de.png" alt="🗞" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> Paper</a></p>								</div>
				</div>
